{"reference":"Revelation 5","book":"Revelation","chapter":5,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Across Revelation","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Revelation repeatedly reworks imagery and language from Israel’s Scriptures, especially Daniel, Ezekiel, Isaiah, Exodus, Zechariah, Genesis, and Psalms. Read within the book’s wider throne visions, the slaughtered Lamb is presented as worthy to open the scroll and to receive worship.","verse_refs":["Revelation 10:1-11","Revelation 11:1-19","Revelation 12:1-17","Revelation 13:1-18","Revelation 14:1-20","Revelation 15:1-8","Revelation 16:1-21","Revelation 17:1-18","Revelation 18:1-24","Revelation 19:1-21","Revelation 1:1-20","Revelation 20:1-15","Revelation 21:1-27","Revelation 22:1-21","Revelation 2:1-29","Revelation 3:1-22","Revelation 4:1-11","Revelation 6:1-17","Revelation 7:1-17","Revelation 8:1-13","Revelation 9:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_005_ff2e6ab70ceaf10f1dc7ed6a"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}